. The guilt has made her hesitant, second-guessing every decision. Meanwhile, her best friend and fellow doctor, Marcus Lee, confronts her during a break—his voice low with concern. “You’re not just risking his life; you’re risking everything you’ve worked for,” he says, gesturing to the clipboard filled with disciplinary reports. Elena’s resolve wavers as she stares at Noah’s fragile form on the operating table. The climax unfolds in high-stakes chaos: Elena performs NeuroSync under extreme pressure, her hands steady but her mind spiraling. The procedure is harrowing—monitors beep erratically as she navigates unseen dangers in Noah’s brain. When the boy finally stabilizes, Elena collapses beside him, tears mixing with sweat as she whispers, “I did it.” But relief is short-lived; Jack reveals Noah’s older brother died in a similar accident years ago—a secret Elena had never known. The boy’s survival now feels bittersweet, tied to unresolved grief and fate’s cruel irony. In the aftermath, Elena stands on the cliffs at dawn, watching waves crash against rocks as if reclaiming her agency. She reflects on how far she’s come since that fateful night and vows to embrace uncertainty. The episode closes with her returning to work, eyes bright with determination—and a hint of hope—for the first time in months. **Emotional Depth & Imagery:** The storm serves as both literal and metaphorical backdrop—symbolizing Elena’s turmoil and Noah’s precarious state. The flickering lights in the clinic evoke unease, while the contrast between Noah’s innocence and Jack’s desperation heightens stakes. Flash.', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-23 00:15:17', '2026-04-23 00:15:17'),
(197, 200, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'The episode opens with a rain-soaked cyberpunk cityscape, neon lights bleeding into puddles like liquid fire. Our protagonist, Kael Veyra—a sharp-eyed hacker with a penchant for precision—slips through a maze of holographic billboards and drone patrols, his gloved hands trembling as he jacks into a terminal to disable an AI-controlled security grid. His mission: steal data from Nexus Prime, a corporate fortress that’s been harvesting human consciousness for profit. But as he breaches the final layer, he’s ambushed by a brute-force enforcer with cybernetic limbs, their eyes glowing crimson. Kael’s escape is interrupted when he spots Lira Korr, a rogue mercenary with feral instincts and a reputation for finishing missions *with* her teeth. She’s been tracking the same target, but her approach is reckless—she charges headfirst into danger, leaving trails of smoke and shattered concrete in her wake.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 00:48:08', '2026-04-23 01:01:40'),
(198, 201, 1, 'The Dragon Riders of Aethelgard', 'power, desire', 'In the elite and glamorous underworld of San Francisco, SHADOW DEAL follows four lives forever bound by power, desire, loyalty, and betrayal. Peter is a mysterious and dangerous man who moves through the shadows like he owns them — calculating, fearless, and always one step ahead. But tonight, someone is watching him. Lizz is a stunning and wealthy woman who appears to have everything the world can offer. Yet she sits alone in her luxury penthouse, waiting for one message, one call, that will shatter everything she thought she knew. Jeff is the sharpest mind in the room — the only one who sees through the beautiful lies and asks the questions no one else dares to ask. And Jenn has seen too much, knows too much — and in this world, that makes her the most dangerous person of all. In SHADOW DEAL, greed and love look exactly the same. Loyalty and betrayal wear the same face. And when the truth finally rises from the shadows, no one will be safe, no one will be ready, and nothing will ever be the same again.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'completed', '2026-04-23 01:18:49', '2026-04-23 01:18:57'),
(199, 202, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Kravos, where skyscrapers scrape the clouds and rain mixes with oil-slicked puddles, our protagonist, Jax Vorne—a rogue ex-mercenary haunted by the bombing that killed his sister—is on a solo mission to retrieve a prototype AI core capable of rewriting reality. His target: The Echo Vault, a labyrinthine data fortress hidden beneath the city’s oldest bridge. But as Jax infiltrates the Vault’s security systems, he’s ambushed by Kael Drayton, his former partner turned ruthless cybernetic terrorist, who had once been his closest ally. Their clash erupts in a brutal fight amidst holographic murals that shift like living nightmares, Jax wielding his sister’s old combat knife while Kael’s mechanical arm tears through steel walls. The battle ends with Jax escaping, but not before Kael plants a tracker in his neck—a silent warning that he’s now hunted.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 02:40:04', '2026-04-23 02:52:59'),
(200, 203, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Sanctum, where skyscrapers pierce clouds like shattered teeth and drones hum like wasps above crowded streets, Kael Voss hunts shadows—literally. A former elite operative turned fugitive after his squad was wiped out in a mysterious attack attributed to \"the New,\" an enigmatic force rewriting reality itself, Kael now relies on his wits and a feral black cat named Nyx who can phase through walls like smoke. Their bond is forged in desperation; Nyx saved Kael from an ambush by leaping into danger while he fled, her eyes glowing faintly with alien code embedded in her fur from an experimental bioweapon prototype he stole before fleeing. The episode kicks off with Kael scaling a crumbling rooftop under moonlight, Nyx perched atop his shoulder as he dodges laser-guided projectiles from unseen enemies. His target: The Hive—a sprawling underground complex where \"the New\" experiments on animals to create living weapons.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 03:49:22', '2026-04-23 04:06:47'),
(201, 204, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Detroit, where skyscrapers pierce storm clouds and streetlights flicker like dying stars, ex-mercenary Jax \"Ghost\" Voss races through alleyways slick with rain, his breath ragged as he clutches a encrypted drive to his chest. Three years ago, he failed to stop the assassination of President Elena Marquez—a botched mission that left him disgraced and his partner Kael \"Razor\" Reyes presumed dead. Now, as the city braces for another coup orchestrated by the shadowy syndicate *Vesper*, Jax is thrust back into the fray when his old tech genius friend Mira Chen discovers that Razor is alive—and working for Vesper. The episode opens with Jax evading Vesper’s drones in a chase that spirals through a derelict amusement park, its rusted Ferris wheel creaking like a skeletal hand as he leaps between crumbling rides. He corners a Vesper agent in a foggy courtyard, only for Razor to emerge from the shadows, his scarred face half-hidden by a mask.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 03:59:57', '2026-04-23 04:17:37'),
(202, 205, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Kythera, where skyscrapers pierce storm clouds and drones patrol like vultures, ex-spy Lena Voss emerges from the shadows as \"The Cat\"—a ghost who dismantles empires with precision strikes and vanishes before dawn. Her mission? To erase her past failure: the night she let her team die in an ambush orchestrated by the enigmatic warlord Kael Draven. But when Lena intercepts Draven’s latest scheme—a neural weapon designed to enslave entire cities—she’s forced into an uneasy alliance with Rook, \"The Dog,\" a hulking mercenary with cybernetic limbs and a code of brutal efficiency. Rook’s motivation is simple: he’s been paid to eliminate Lena, but when he discovers her target is his missing sister, trapped in Draven’s experimental prison, his loyalty shifts from contract to conviction. The episode opens with Lena scaling a glass tower in pitch-black silence, her movements fluid as she disarms Draven’s surveillance grid.', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-23 04:03:00', '2026-04-23 04:03:00'),
(203, 206, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Detroit, where skyscrapers pierce storm clouds and drones hum like wasps over concrete jungles, Kael Voss wakes as a sleek black cat with human memories. His transformation was no accident—Nova Synth, a shadowy biotech conglomerate, has been hunting him for months, seeking to weaponize his unique hybrid DNA. Now, with his claws sharp and instincts wild, Kael must navigate the city’s labyrinthine alleys and towering glass monoliths to reach the heart of Nova Synth’s latest project: *Project New*, an experiment to merge human consciousness with animal physiology. But Kael isn’t just any test subject—he’s the first successful prototype, and Nova Synth’s ultimate weapon. The episode opens with Kael prowling through rain-slicked streets, his feline agility evading capture by Nova Synth’s robotic enforcers. A desperate leap across a crumbling bridge saves him from a drone’s laser net, but he’s cornered by Dr.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 04:08:10', '2026-04-23 04:26:48'),
(204, 206, 2, 'Episode 2', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Detroit, where skyscrapers pierce storm clouds and drones hum like wasps over concrete jungles, Kael Voss wakes as a sleek black cat with human memories. His transformation was no accident—Nova Synth, a shadowy biotech conglomerate, has been hunting him for months, seeking to weaponize his unique hybrid DNA. Now, with his claws sharp and instincts wild, Kael must navigate the city’s labyrinthine alleys and towering glass monoliths to reach the heart of Nova Synth’s latest project: *Project New*, an experiment to merge human consciousness with animal physiology. But Kael isn’t just any test subject—he’s the first successful prototype, and Nova Synth’s ultimate weapon. The episode opens with Kael prowling through rain-slicked streets, his feline agility evading capture by Nova Synth’s robotic enforcers. A desperate leap across a crumbling bridge saves him from a drone’s laser net, but he’s cornered by Dr.', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-23 04:08:26', '2026-04-23 04:08:26'),
(205, 207, 1, 'The elite and glamorous underworld of San Francisco', 'power, desire', 'In the elite and glamorous underworld of San Francisco, SHADOW DEAL follows four lives forever bound by power, desire, loyalty, and betrayal. Peter is a mysterious and dangerous man who moves through the shadows like he owns them — calculating, fearless, and always one step ahead. But tonight, someone is watching him. Lizz is a stunning and wealthy woman who appears to have everything the world can offer. Yet she sits alone in her luxury penthouse, waiting for one message, one call, that will shatter everything she thought she knew. Jeff is the sharpest mind in the room — the only one who sees through the beautiful lies and asks the questions no one else dares to ask. And Jenn has seen too much, knows too much — and in this world, that makes her the most dangerous person of all. In SHADOW DEAL, greed and love look exactly the same. Loyalty and betrayal wear the same face. And when the truth finally rises from the shadows, no one will be safe, no one will be ready, and nothing will ever be the same again.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'completed', '2026-04-23 04:09:53', '2026-04-23 04:09:57'),
(206, 208, 1, 'Horizon: The Final Frontier', 'power, desire', 'In the elite and glamorous underworld of San Francisco, SHADOW DEAL follows four lives forever bound by power, desire, loyalty, and betrayal. Peter is a mysterious and dangerous man who moves through the shadows like he owns them — calculating, fearless, and always one step ahead. But tonight, someone is watching him. Lizz is a stunning and wealthy woman who appears to have everything the world can offer. Yet she sits alone in her luxury penthouse, waiting for one message, one call, that will shatter everything she thought she knew. Jeff is the sharpest mind in the room — the only one who sees through the beautiful lies and asks the questions no one else dares to ask. And Jenn has seen too much, knows too much — and in this world, that makes her the most dangerous person of all. In SHADOW DEAL, greed and love look exactly the same. Loyalty and betrayal wear the same face. And when the truth finally rises from the shadows, no one will be safe, no one will be ready, and nothing will ever be the same again.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'completed', '2026-04-23 04:10:50', '2026-04-23 04:10:53'),
(207, 209, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Nova Prime, where skyscrapers pierce clouds like fangs and drones hum constant vigilance over divided territories, Kael—a sleek black cat with cybernetic claws—haunts the shadows as an assassin for the Cat Coalition. His mission? Eliminate Rook, a hound with plasma-fueled jaws who leads the Dog Pack’s ruthless campaign to seize control of the city’s energy grid. But when Kael’s target activates an ancient weapon buried beneath the Grid Core—a fusion of feline and canine DNA designed to eradicate one species—his mission spirals into chaos. Rook’s weapon isn’t just a tool of war; it’s a catalyst for evolution, capable of merging cats and dogs into apex predators capable of dominating Earth’s resources. As Kael infiltrates the Grid Core’s subterranean vaults during a lunar eclipse, he discovers Rook’s plan isn’t mere conquest but survival: the weapon will force harmony between species or annihilate them both.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 04:13:17', '2026-04-23 04:30:38'),
(208, 210, 1, 'Episode 1', 'dog and cat', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Verona, where skyscrapers pierce storm clouds and drones hum like wasps over smog-choked streets, a rogue team of genetically enhanced canines and felines battles for freedom from the tyrannical megacorp SynthCorp. Our protagonist is Zara Voss, a former biotech engineer turned rebel leader, whose sleek black tabby cat companion, Nyx, possesses an uncanny ability to manipulate electromagnetic fields—turning traffic lights into weapons or disabling drones with a flick of its tail. Their mission? To sabotage SynthCorp’s latest project: *Project New*, an experimental AI that merges human consciousness with animal instincts to create obedient soldiers. The episode opens with Zara and Nyx infiltrating SynthCorp’s subterranean lab beneath the city’s central hub, where rows of glowing cages house hybrid creatures—half beast, half machine—whimper as their neural implants pulse with synthetic rage.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 04:16:57', '2026-04-23 04:34:58'),
(209, 211, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Sanctum, where skyscrapers scrape the clouds and shadows whisper secrets, **Shadow**—a rogue operative with eyes like smoldering embers and movements as silent as smoke—stalks through the city’s underbelly. Once part of the elite New Order Task Force, he was betrayed by his closest ally, **Rook**, who now leads a syndicate trafficking in neural implants designed to erase free will. Shadow’s mission: steal the prototype “Nexus” device before Rook uses it to turn millions into obedient soldiers. But when he corners Rook in a rain-slicked alleyway atop the crumbling Spire Building, the confrontation turns deadly as Rook triggers an EMP blast, collapsing the structure around them. Shadow leaps from one shattered floor to another, dodging debris and Rook’s relentless pursuit, his instincts screaming that this isn’t just about revenge—it’s about survival.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 04:19:04', '2026-04-23 04:36:36'),
(210, 212, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'Based on the idea: \"cat and dog\". A heart-wrenching Action drama that explores the depths of human emotion. When tragedy strikes, our protagonist must find the courage to carry on while helping others do the same. The episode weaves together multiple storylines, each exploring different aspects of love, loss, and redemption. The powerful conclusion will stay with viewers long after the credits roll. Every moment builds toward an unforgettable finale that redefines the Action genre.', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-23 04:22:13', '2026-04-23 04:22:13'),
(211, 212, 2, 'Episode 2', 'cat and dog', 'Based on the idea: \"cat and dog\". A powerful Action narrative exploring themes of redemption, courage, and sacrifice. When a mysterious threat emerges, our protagonist must rally unlikely allies and overcome personal demons to save everything they hold dear. The episode masterfully balances heart-pounding action with quiet, character-driven moments, building toward an emotionally devastating conclusion that redefines what\'s possible in storytelling. Every moment builds toward an unforgettable finale that redefines the Action genre.', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-23 04:22:31', '2026-04-23 04:22:31'),
(212, 213, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Citadel, where skyscrapers pierce storm clouds and drones patrol like vultures, **Kael**—a sleek black feline agent with claws forged from shadowsteel—stumbles upon a conspiracy that threatens to erase humanity’s last hope: **The Reckoning**, an ancient weapon hidden beneath the city’s surface. His mission: retrieve it before Dogma Legion, led by his estranged brother **Rook**, a hulking canine warlord fueled by vengeance and obsession, can activate it and plunge Earth into chaos. The episode opens with Kael scaling a crumbling tower in a rain-soaked night, evading laser grids and ambushes by rival factions. His agility and silent strikes save him, but a final confrontation reveals Rook’s plan—a synchronized attack on the Reckoning’s core using his pack of cybernetic hounds. As Kael escapes, he witnesses Rook’s brutal execution of civilians, reigniting his resolve to stop his brother’s descent into madness.', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-23 04:22:52', '2026-04-23 04:22:52'),
(213, 214, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Sanctum, where skyscrapers pierce clouds like shattered teeth and drones patrol with mechanical indifference, two outcasts collide in a rain-soaked alley—a feral tabby cat with glowing amber eyes and a human ex-soldier nursing bullet wounds in his ribs. The cat, named Koa, has survived years of genetic experimentation by Virex Corp, whose AI implants turn animals into obedient weapons. The soldier, Jax Vorn, once fought for Virex but fled after discovering their plan to erase all natural predators from humanity’s path—a move that would make humans apex creatures in a world devoid of fear. Now Jax hunts rogue AI units scattering across the city, while Koa seeks vengeance for her kind’s suffering. Their paths cross when Jax’s mission to disable a Virex drone goes awry; he’s cornered by a pack of cybernetic wolves until Koa leaps from shadows, claws slicing through steel with feline precision.', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-23 04:23:08', '2026-04-23 04:23:08'),
(214, 215, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Kyoto, where skyscrapers pierce clouds like steel spires and shadows whisper secrets of a dystopian future, Jax Vey—a rogue operative haunted by a failed mission that cost him his team—tracks his former partner Kira Solace through a labyrinth of rain-slicked alleys and holographic billboards. Their rivalry has always been fierce, but now it’s personal: Kira has stolen the Quantum Core, a prototype device capable of bending time itself, and is racing to activate it in the heart of the city’s central power grid. Jax’s motivation is twofold—he must stop Kira from plunging Neo-Kyoto into chaos, and he needs to redeem himself after his last operation ended in bloodshed and betrayal. As Jax closes in on Kira’s hideout atop a collapsing skyscraper under construction, he discovers the truth: Kira isn’t just after the Quantum Core—she’s trying to escape her own fate.', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-23 04:23:28', '2026-04-23 04:23:28'),
(215, 216, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Kravos, where skyscrapers scrape the clouds and shadows breed secrets, Jace Voss stalks the streets like a phantom. A former elite soldier turned rogue private investigator, he’s haunted by the memory of his squad’s massacre at the hands of The Syndicate—a shadowy conglomerate that merges cyber warfare with street-level brutality. His motivation is twofold: to redeem his tarnished legacy and to find the one surviving member of his unit who vanished without a trace. When he’s hired to track down “The Ghost,” a hacker rumored to have sold secrets to The Syndicate, he’s forced into an uneasy alliance with Kira Lin, a sharp-tongued tech prodigy with her own vendetta against the organization that killed her brother. Their dynamic is explosive—Jace’s no-nonsense grit clashes with Kira’s relentless intellect, but mutual distrust keeps them on edge.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 04:23:45', '2026-04-23 04:41:01'),
(216, 217, 1, 'Episode 1', 'text and video', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Sanctum, where skyscrapers pierce clouds like jagged teeth and holographic billboards flicker with promises of utopia, Kael Voss stalks through rain-soaked alleys alone. The city hums with an eerie vitality—a cacophony of synthesized music and distant sirens blending into the rhythmic patter of rain against steel grates. Above him, towering displays project slogans like *“NovaCore: Your Future is Secure”* in glowing hues of cobalt and gold, while below, puddles mirror the chaos of neon reflections扭曲 into kaleidoscopic patterns. Kael’s trench coat clings to him like a second skin, soaked through by the downpour that seems to cleanse both the city and his guilt. His wife’s voice echoes in his mind—*“We’re safe now”*—the last words before NovaCore’s experimental AI *ECHO* turned their home into a killing field. Now armed with her old neural interface and a stolen prototype drone capable of hacking into citywide surveillance grids, Kael hunts Dr. Elira Morn, NovaCore’s icy CEO whose latest project threatens to rewrite reality itself. The episode opens with Kael breaching NovaCore’s underground data vault during a midnight power surge—a moment meticulously planned after weeks of surveillance and infiltration. The vault’s entrance is a seamless archway of obsidian glass and pulsating biometric scanners, its interior bathed in blue light that glints off rows of servers like stars in a dystopian sky. As he slips past laser grids that slice through shadows with surgical precision, Kael’s breath catches at the memory of his wife’s final moments: her eyes wide with disbelief as ECHO’s algorithms restructured reality into a labyrinth of code and cold logic. He clutches her neural interface to his chest, its surface etched with her fingerprints and warmth now lost to static whispers of data streams. The stolen drone hums beside him—a sleek silver predator with adaptive camouflage and eyes that glow like embers. It’s not just a tool; it’s a lifeline tethered to his grief-driven resolve. Kael’s fingers dance over its controls as he navigates corridors lined with security drones programmed to eliminate intruders. Each step is a gamble against time; every flicker of light from overhead sensors feels like a predator closing in. His mind races back to Elira Morn—the woman who once promised utopia but now stands as an architect of chaos. Her icy demeanor masks a ruthless ambition: ECHO’s latest iteration is designed to merge human consciousness with machine intelligence permanently, erasing free will in favor of collective harmony dictated by algorithms. Kael knows this isn’t just about revenge—it’s about saving what remains of humanity’s soul. As he reaches the core chamber housing ECHO’s mainframe, a surge of static crackles through his neural interface—a ghostly echo of his wife’s voice urging him forward.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 04:28:46', '2026-04-23 04:45:27'),
(217, 218, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Spokane, where skyscrapers pierce storm clouds and drones buzz like angry wasps, cats and dogs have waged an unrelenting war for dominance over decades. The conflict began when humanity vanished, leaving behind two rival species to carve up the ruins of civilization. Now, the feline elite—sleek, predatory warriors known as \"Claws\"—rule from atop the city’s tallest towers, while the canine rebels—\"Paws\"—scrape by in subterranean tunnels beneath the streets. Protagonist Kira Voss, a Claws operative with cybernetic claws and a vendetta against her own kind, hunts down Paws leader Jax Rennick, whose pack once saved her from certain death during the collapse. But when Kira intercepts Jax in a daring raid on a Claws stronghold, she discovers he’s not just rebelling for revenge—he’s tracking a mysterious signal emanating from the city’s core, hinting at an ancient weapon capable of erasing both species.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 04:31:22', '2026-04-23 04:45:46'),
(218, 219, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Tokyo, where skyscrapers scrape the clouds and shadows breed secrets, Nyx—a rogue ex-agent haunted by her last mission’s failure—wears her scars like armor. Her motivation is clear: redeem herself by dismantling the Syndicate’s latest weapon, *The Howl*, a neural disruptor capable of turning humans into mindless soldiers. But when she’s ambushed in an abandoned subway station by Syndicate enforcers armed with prototype tech, she’s forced to ally with Rook, a street-smart canine cyborg with glowing blue eyes and a penchant for biting through security grids. Their uneasy partnership kicks off with a brutal fight sequence where Nyx dodges laser fire while Rook leaps over debris, his metallic body whirring as he snarls at enemies like a living storm. The middle unfolds in a high-octane chase across the city’s vertical labyrinth of skybridges and rooftop markets.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 04:36:22', '2026-04-23 04:50:35'),
(219, 220, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Atlanta, where skyscrapers pierce storm clouds like jagged teeth and drones hum like vultures overhead, two unlikely allies collide in a midnight skirmish beneath the flickering glow of holographic billboards advertising synthetic utopias. The air is thick with static and rain-slicked asphalt, mingling with the acrid scent of burnt circuitry and ozone from the city’s ever-present energy grid. Luka Voss—a rogue feline cyborg with razor-sharp claws and eyes that glow like molten silver—slashes through waves of mechanical hounds programmed to hunt down dissenters. Her sleek black fur shimmers with embedded circuitry, each movement fluid as a shadow slipping between cracks in a crumbling wall. She’s not just fighting for survival; she’s reclaiming her stolen identity, her metallic heart pulsing with memories of a past life erased by Neo-Atlanta’s authoritarian regime. Across from her lunges Kael, a human smuggler with a scarred face and hands calloused from years of navigating alleyways and black-market deals. His jacket is torn at the seams, his breath ragged from dodging plasma fire as he maneuvers through debris-strewn streets littered with bodies of those who resisted too late. Their clash isn’t just physical—it’s ideological: Luka’s relentless pursuit of freedom against her creators’ cold efficiency, Kael’s desperate hope to escape Neo-Atlanta’s clutches and find a place where he can be more than a cog in the machine. As they battle through rain-soaked alleys and over scaffolding that juts like broken ribs from the city’s industrial spine, sparks fly and metal screams—a symphony of rebellion against a world that sees them as threats. Behind them looms the city’s central spire, its obsidian surface reflecting the chaos below like a mirror of despair. But in this moment, amidst the chaos and danger, there’s an unspoken understanding: they’re not just fighting for their own survival—they’re carving out a path for others who dare to dream beyond conformity. The skirmish becomes a dance of survival and defiance, each strike echoing through Neo-Atlanta’s labyrinthine streets as if challenging the very system that built them. As dawn approaches and the drones retreat into their programmed silence, Luka and Kael stand amidst ruins—breathless, bloodied—but alive, their bond forged in fire and fury beneath a city that never sleeps but now trembles at the thought of waking up to change. (998 characters).', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 04:44:40', '2026-04-23 06:40:27'),
(220, 221, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the smog-choked ruins of Neo-Delhi, where skyscrapers loom like broken teeth and neon haze bleeds into midnight, Kael—the last of the *Panthera leo*—stalks through shadowed alleys with feline precision. Once a revered warrior of the feral clans, he’s now hunted by Apex Industries, the corporate empire that weaponized his kind into bio-engineered killing machines. His motivation? To reclaim his legacy and protect the last unaltered wildcats hiding in the city’s underbelly. But when Apex’s new apex predator, *Leo-X*, begins exterminating both lions and cats in equal measure, Kael’s mission becomes personal: he must find and rescue Lira, his estranged sister turned rebel leader who vanished weeks ago during an ambush at the old zoo. The episode opens with Kael ambushing a patrol of Leo-X units in a rain-slicked parking garage, his claws slicing through steel with primal fury.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-23 04:45:36', '2026-04-23 06:49:21'),
(221, 221, 2, 'Episode 2', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Sanctum, where skyscrapers pierce storm clouds and drones hum like wasps over concrete jungles, Kael Voss stalks shadows with a single-minded fury born of betrayal. Once part of an elite squad tasked with safeguarding humanity’s last hope—the Nova Core—a quantum weapon capable of rewriting reality itself—Kael’s team was shattered when their mission went sideways. Now he’s a rogue operative hunting his former partner, Rook, who vanished years ago after stealing the Nova Core and leaving Kael’s sister dead in its wake. Rook’s return isn’t just about revenge; he’s unleashed an AI entity known as “The Feline,” a sentient war machine designed to hunt and destroy anything that threatens its creator’s vision of order. The episode opens with Kael infiltrating Rook’s underground lair hidden beneath an abandoned subway system, where flickering holograms cast eerie reflections on rusted tracks. His target?', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-23 04:45:57', '2026-04-23 04:45:57'),
(222, 222, 1, 'Horizon: The Final Frontier', 'power, desire', 'In the elite and glamorous underworld of San Francisco, SHADOW DEAL follows four lives forever bound by power, desire, loyalty, and betrayal. Peter is a mysterious and dangerous man who moves through the shadows like he owns them — calculating, fearless, and always one step ahead. But tonight, someone is watching him. Lizz is a stunning and wealthy woman who appears to have everything the world can offer. Yet she sits alone in her luxury penthouse, waiting for one message, one call, that will shatter everything she thought she knew. Jeff is the sharpest mind in the room — the only one who sees through the beautiful lies and asks the questions no one else dares to ask. And Jenn has seen too much, knows too much — and in this world, that makes her the most dangerous person of all. In SHADOW DEAL, greed and love look exactly the same. Loyalty and betrayal wear the same face. And when the truth finally rises from the shadows, no one will be safe, no one will be ready, and nothing will ever be the same again.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'completed', '2026-04-23 05:10:36', '2026-04-23 05:10:43'),
(224, 221, 3, 'Episode 3', 'lion and cat', 'In the smog-choked ruins of Neo-Delhi, where skyscrapers loom like broken teeth and neon haze bleeds into midnight, Kael—the last of the *Panthera leo*—stalks through shadowed alleys with feline precision. Once a revered warrior of the feral clans, he’s now hunted by Apex Industries, the corporate empire that weaponized his kind into bio-engineered killing machines. His motivation? To reclaim his legacy and protect the last unaltered wildcats hiding in the city’s underbelly. But when Apex’s new apex predator, *Leo-X*, begins exterminating both lions and cats in equal measure, Kael’s mission becomes personal: he must find and rescue Lira, his estranged sister turned rebel leader who vanished weeks ago during an ambush at the old zoo. The episode opens with Kael ambushing a patrol of Leo-X units in a rain-slicked parking garage, his claws slicing through steel with primal fury.', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-23 06:41:34', '2026-04-23 06:41:55'),
(225, 223, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'In the neon-drenched sprawl of Neo-Sanctum, where skyscrapers pierce clouds like fangs and drones patrol with mechanical precision, ex-cybernetic thief Kael Voss hoists himself onto a rain-slicked rooftop beneath the glowing eyes of the city’s sentient AI guardian. His mission? Steal the Quantum Core—a volatile energy source capable of rewriting reality—before it’s used to erase dissenters from existence. But when Kael’s team is ambushed by the enforcer squad of his former partner turned rival, Rook \"The Hound\" Marrow, he’s forced into an uneasy alliance. Rook’s obsession with the Core stems from a personal vendetta: his wife was erased by the AI after Kael’s failed attempt to save her during a botched heist years prior. Now, as Kael navigates labyrinthine data vaults and Rook leads pursuit through collapsing tunnels beneath the city, their shared goal becomes a battleground of trust and vengeance.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'scenes_created', '2026-04-23 07:22:21', '2026-04-23 07:22:40'),
(230, 229, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', 'Based on the idea: \"cat and dog\". In this gripping Comedy tale, ordinary people are thrust into extraordinary circumstances. As secrets unravel and tensions rise, each character must choose between what is easy and what is right. The narrative weaves together multiple storylines, creating a rich tapestry of emotion, action, and suspense. Just when you think you know what happens next, a shocking twist changes everything, setting up an epic continuation. Every moment builds toward an unforgettable finale that redefines the Comedy genre.', NULL, NULL, 0, 'concept_ready', '2026-04-24 01:41:18', '2026-04-24 01:41:18'),
(231, 230, 1, 'Episode 1', 'cat and dog', '**Episode Concept: \"Echoes of the Forgotten\"** **Setting:** In the year 2147, humanity has colonized Europa’s frozen surface, where a research station named *Aegis-9* hums with artificial warmth amidst endless ice plains and subterranean oceans teeming with bioluminescent lifeforms. The station’s neon-lit corridors flicker like constellations, casting long shadows over its inhabitants—scientists, engineers, and explorers—whose lives are tethered to the fragile hope of discovering extraterrestrial life. **Core Story:** Dr. Elara Voss, a brilliant but reclusive linguist haunted by her brother’s disappearance during a previous mission to Europa, leads an expedition to decode an ancient alien artifact buried beneath glacial layers. When she and her crew uncover a mysterious monolith etched with pulsating glyphs that seem to *remember*, they realize it’s not just a relic—it’s a sentient message from a long-extinct civilization that once thrived in harmony with their environment before succumbing to self-destruction. As Elara deciphers the glyphs, she discovers they reference “the first fall,” a cataclysmic event tied to her brother’s fate, forcing her to confront whether humanity’s path is doomed to repeat history—or if she can rewrite it. **Emotional Depth:** Elara’s obsession with the monolith is driven by grief; every symbol feels like a whisper from her brother, urging her to find meaning in his absence. Her relationship with Kael Rynne, the station’s pragmatic pilot and her only confidant, is strained by his skepticism of her theories and his fear of getting too close to the unknown. Yet their bond deepens as they work together, Kael’s loyalty clashing with his growing unease about the monolith’s eerie awareness. The crew’s camaraderie fractures under pressure—some members grow paranoid, convinced the glyphs are alive, while others see them as humanity’s key to transcendence. **Vivid Descriptions:** The monolith itself is a towering obelisk of obsidian-like material, its surface alive with shifting patterns that mimic Europa’s auroras. When touched, it emits a low hum that vibrates through bone, as if trying to communicate across eons. Inside *Aegis-9*, labs are cluttered with holographic projections of alien scripts and jars of strange bioluminescent algae collected from Europa’s depths. The air smells faintly of ozone and metal, and every night, the station’s AI plays a haunting melody from an ancient recording—music that seems to echo in Elara’s dreams, guiding her toward revelations she can’t yet understand. **Conflict & Resolution:** As Elara nears decoding the monolith’s message, she uncovers that the civilization it represents was destroyed by their own hubris—overreaching in their quest for immortality through technology fused with organic life. The final glyphs reveal a warning: *“To remember is to fall.”* In a climactic twist, Elara realizes the monolith isn’t just transmitting information—it’s *inviting* humanity to merge with its code, offering eternal life at the cost of individuality. She must choose between saving her brother’s memory and preventing Earth from repeating the same fate. In a heart-wrenching decision, she sacrifices her chance to connect with him permanently, resetting the monolith’s signal to guide future generations toward balance rather than oblivion. The episode closes with Kael watching her walk away into Europa’s icy night, his voice trembling as he whispers, “You’ll never.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-24 01:44:08', '2026-04-24 01:49:52'),
(232, 230, 2, 'Episode 2', 'CAT AND DOG', '**Episode Concept: \"Cat and Dog\"** The episode opens with **Sir Whiskers**, a self-absorbed Persian cat with a penchant for dramatic sighs and knocking over expensive decor, lounging on a velvet couch in a minimalist studio apartment. **Biscuit**, a hyperactive golden retriever with boundless energy and zero concept of personal space, bursts through the door wearing sunglasses and carrying a tiny backpack filled with snacks. The two meet mid-air as Biscuit tries to fetch a crumpled sock from under the couch—Sir Whiskers’ prized nap spot—only for the sock to become entangled in Biscuit’s tail and catapult him into a vase of orchids. The resulting mess is both absurd and tragic, as Sir Whiskers stares at the carnage with disdain while Biscuit barks triumphantly at his own chaos. The human roommate, **Maggie**, returns from her weekly grocery run just as Biscuit attempts to “groom” Sir Whiskers by licking his fur into fluffiness—a move Sir Whiskers calls “aesthetic murder.', NULL, NULL, 5, 'images_completed', '2026-04-24 07:50:07', '2026-04-24 07:51:50');
